<http://data.silknow.org/object/2774eeec-43ac-3c3e-ae72-804fd549a854/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Probably from a valance, Suppliant woman. Embroidered with polychrome crewels and silks in tent stitch on linen canvas ground. Foreground shows woman kneeling before another woman in what appears to be a garden. At left, stream runs throug middle ground and a group of figures stands before a turreted building. Various birds and flowers are shown. Figures in period costume of late 16th century. Condition good with a few repairs. Lining and edging later additions."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/2774eeec-43ac-3c3e-ae72-804fd549a854> .

